# CUSTOMER INGRESS
# Apply to customer-facing ports / VLANs (resi, DIA, GPON, etc.)
# Direction: inbound from customer toward AS396952
#
# Intent: allow on-link discovery (ARP / DHCP / DHCPv6), then only
# forward traffic sourced from net253 netblocks. Everything else drops
# (spoofed foreign space, martians, etc.).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ALLOWLISTS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Keep in sync with owned / announced space (bgp/net253_bgp.yml)
NET253_V4 =
  23.140.108.0/24 ||
  142.248.74.0/24 ||
  142.248.75.0/24 ||
  192.69.184.0/22 ||
  199.36.252.0/22 ||
  204.238.8.0/24 ||
  208.87.163.0/24

NET253_V6 =
  2602:fec2::/32

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# POLICY (pseudocode)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

apply to CUSTOMER_INGRESS ports

# 1) On-link discovery — must work before the host has an address
if (ethertype == ARP)
  accept comment="ARP"

# DHCPv4: discover/request from 0.0.0.0, replies to broadcast, etc.
if (udp dst-port == 67 || udp dst-port == 68)
  accept comment="DHCPv4"

# DHCPv6: clients usually speak from link-local (fe80::/10)
if (udp dst-port == 546 || udp dst-port == 547)
  accept comment="DHCPv6"

# 2) Customer data plane — only packets sourced from our space
if (src in NET253_V4 || src in NET253_V6)
  accept comment="sourced from net253 netblock"

# 3) Everything else is spoofed / foreign / improper
drop comment="not ARP/DHCP and not from net253"
